<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Prediq's four pages. Hand-written rather than generated, because four URLs do
  not justify a build step in a project whose whole premise is not having one.

  NO lastmod. Three of these pages change every time the archive does, several
  times a day, and this file does not. A lastmod written once and then left is
  worse than none at all: it invites a crawler to skip a page that has in fact
  changed, and it is a date this project cannot honestly maintain by hand.
  Omitting the field says "I do not know", which is true.

  NO priority or changefreq either. Both are hints search engines stopped acting
  on years ago, and inventing a ranking among four pages would be a statement
  about importance that nothing here supports.

  Add a page, add it here. An incomplete sitemap is a quiet way to keep something
  out of an index.

  One thing to know before editing this comment: a double hyphen is illegal inside
  an XML comment, and unlike HTML nothing tolerates it. The whole file becomes
  unparseable, which a crawler reports to nobody. Use an em dash.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url><loc>https://prediq.top/</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://prediq.top/record.html</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://prediq.top/ratings.html</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://prediq.top/method.html</loc></url>
</urlset>
